# Chapter Summary

Threat hunting extends the capabilities of a Security Operations Center beyond automated alerting by enabling analysts to proactively search for suspicious activity. Using Microsoft Sentinel and Kusto Query Language, analysts can investigate authentication events, identify indicators of compromise, validate hypotheses, and improve future detection strategies.

In this project, threat hunting focused on SSH authentication logs, leading to the identification of repeated failed login attempts and supporting the development of detection rules for brute-force activity.

